# Crypto Watcher — Backend

> Phase tags (`MVP`, `Phase 1`, `Phase 2`, `Phase 3`, `Final`) cite
> [ROADMAP](./ROADMAP.mdc). On-chain logic lives in [CONTRACTS](./CONTRACTS.mdc);
> the API consumed by the UI is in [FRONTEND](./FRONTEND.mdc). Keep this file in
> sync with the actual `apps/api/` implementation (see the docs-sync rule in
> `.cursor/rules/`).

## Tech Stack

From the [README](../README.md): Express + Zod, Kysely + PostgreSQL, Node + tsx,
Vitest + Supertest, Docker, Pino + Pino-pretty, and OpenAPI docs generated from
Zod schemas via `@asteasolutions/zod-to-openapi` with Swagger UI. Monorepo via Nx
+ pnpm.

> **Product model:** Official risk scores are published by vetted governors/admins only.
> Regular users submit evidence, report incidents and discuss — but do not influence
> the final score via tokens or public voting. Legacy `voting/` and reputation-weighted
> score paths remain from an earlier design and are being refactored.

## Modular Folder Structure

The API is organized into self-contained modules. Each module owns its routes,
service, repository (Kysely), Zod schemas and tests. Shared concerns live under
`core/` and `shared/`.

