> Each module is independent: routes → service → repository. Modules never import
> another module's repository directly; they call the other module's service.

## Modules by Phase

### projects `[MVP]`
- CRUD + lifecycle state machine matching the README flow
  (`In analysis → Under review → Report published`).
- Read expert-published project score for display.
- Community submission queue. `[Phase 2]`

### comments `[MVP]`
- Public off-chain comments (read all, post when authenticated).

### auth + users `[MVP]`
- Wallet connect + SIWE-style verification, session issuance.
- Email/password registration and login with bcrypt-hashed passwords.
- Email verification and password-reset OTP emails via `packages/email-templates` + `core/mail` (Nodemailer/MailHog). Templates always use the web app dark palette and embed `/logo.png` from `WEB_URL`.
- Link wallet public key to email account.
- Profile management (nickname, X account, avatar, bio).
- Role-based access control + admin console. `[Phase 2]`

### analysis-requests `[MVP]`
- Authenticated users submit projects for team analysis.
- Public listing with status filter; team/admin review workflow.

### voting `[MVP]` (legacy — migrating to governor reviews)
- Index on-chain review registry events from per-project contracts (via `core/chain`).
- Legacy public vote tallies retained until refactor completes.
- Subgraph/indexer ingestion replacing direct RPC reads. `[Phase 2]`

### scoring `[MVP]`
- Serve governor-published project scores and structured report breakdown.
- Scores immutable per review round; methodology version referenced.
- Enrich with external risk-data providers to assist governors. `[Phase 3]`

### market `[MVP]`
- `GET /market/projects/:slug` — USD spot price, 24h/7d/1m/1y change, and up to 1 year of chart history for curated reference slugs.
- Data sourced from CoinGecko (free public API); responses cached in PostgreSQL (`market_cache`) for 3 hours, with in-memory L1 cache and stale DB fallback when CoinGecko is unavailable.
- Slug → CoinGecko ID mapping with overrides for assets whose slug differs (e.g. `xrp` → `ripple`).

### governance — launch requirement
- Read/serve on-chain proposals, votes and outcomes from the Governor. `[MVP]`
- Index governance lifecycle events for the UI + notifications. `[MVP]`
- Community proposal support metadata. `[Phase 1]`
- Delegation data. `[Phase 2]`
- Full DAO/treasury data surfaces. `[Final]`

### reputation `[MVP → Phase 1]`
- Serve governor/reviewer credentials + council accountability metrics. `[MVP]`
- Multi-factor reviewer reputation + decay jobs. `[Phase 1]`

### rewards `[Phase 1]`
- Reviewer compensation and misconduct penalty records, synced with on-chain distributor.

### notifications `[Phase 1]`
- In-app + email (React Email/Nodemailer) for lifecycle + governance events.

### Platform & scaling
- API docs via Zod-generated OpenAPI + Swagger UI. `[MVP]`
- Observability: Sentry + Better Stack, structured Pino logs. `[MVP]`
- Caching + rate limiting + read scaling. `[Phase 2]`
- Public API, API keys. `[Phase 3]`
- Outbound webhooks. `[Phase 3]`
- Multi-region HA. `[Final]`

## Functional Requirements (by module & phase)

### projects `[MVP]`
- R1: Team can create/update a project and transition its lifecycle state.
- R2: Anyone can list/read projects, filter by state/chain, paginate.
- R3: Each project exposes an expert-published score once `Report published`.
- R4: Community submission queue with team review. `[Phase 2]`

### comments `[MVP]`
- R1: Anyone can read comments for a project.
- R2: Authenticated users can create comments; authors can soft-delete their own.
- R3: Rate limiting + basic spam protection. `[Phase 2]`

### auth + users `[MVP]`
- R1: Wallet connect with SIWE-style nonce → signature → session.
- R2: Email/password register and login with revocable sessions.
- R3: Sessions are httpOnly-cookie based and revocable.
- R4: Users have a profile (display name, avatar, bio, nickname, X account).
- R5: Users can link a wallet address to an email account.
- R6: Role-based access control (admin/team/user). `[Phase 2]`

### analysis-requests `[MVP]`
- R1: Authenticated users create analysis requests for new projects.
- R2: Anyone can list requests filtered by status.
- R3: Team/admin can update status and add review notes.

### voting `[MVP]` (legacy)
- R1: Legacy public vote index retained for migration; new work uses governor-only scoring.
- R2: Backend indexes on-chain registry events per project.
- R3: Public users cannot publish or amend official scores. `[MVP]`

### scoring `[MVP]`
- R1: Serve governor-published score + breakdown once review is complete.
- R2: Score is immutable per review round and methodology version.
- R3: Enrich with external risk signals for governor analysis. `[Phase 3]`

### governance `[MVP]` — launch requirement
- R1: Index governance proposals, votes and outcomes from the Governor.
- R2: Serve proposal detail + status to the UI.
- R3: Emit notifications on governance lifecycle events. `[Phase 1]`

### reputation `[MVP → Phase 1]`
- R1: Serve reviewer credentials + council membership for governors. `[MVP]`
- R2: Recompute multi-factor reviewer accountability on a schedule. `[Phase 1]`

### rewards `[Phase 1]` / notifications `[Phase 1]`
- R1: Record reviewer compensation / misconduct events synced with on-chain distributor.
- R2: Deliver in-app + email notifications for lifecycle/governance events.

## SQL Data Modeling (PostgreSQL via Kysely)

> Migrations live in `core/db/migrations`; types are generated into
> `core/db/schema.ts`. All ids are `uuid` (default `gen_random_uuid()`), all tables
> carry `created_at timestamptz not null default now()` and (where mutable)
> `updated_at timestamptz`. Addresses are stored lowercase `text` (checksummed in UI).

### `users` `[MVP]`
| column | type | notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| id | uuid pk | |
| wallet_address | text unique | lowercase; nullable for email-only accounts |
| email | text unique | nullable |
| password_hash | text | nullable; bcrypt for email auth |
| public_key | text | linked wallet address |
| x_account | text | nullable |
| nickname | text unique | nullable |
| display_name | text | |
| avatar_url | text | HTTPS URL or `data:image/...;base64,...`; max **256 KB** (`users_avatar_url_length_chk`) |
| bio | text | |
| role | text not null default 'user' | `user` \| `team` \| `admin` `[Phase 2]` |
| email_verified_at | timestamptz | nullable; set after OTP email verification |

### `sessions` `[MVP]`
| column | type | notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| id | uuid pk | |
