## REST API Endpoints

> All routes are Express handlers validated with Zod; schemas feed OpenAPI via
> `@asteasolutions/zod-to-openapi`. `🔒` = authenticated, `👑` = team/admin role
> `[Phase 2]`.

### auth `[MVP]`
- `POST /auth/nonce` → `{ nonce }` for a wallet address.
- `POST /auth/verify` → verify SIWE signature, set session cookie.
- `POST /auth/register` → email/password registration; sends a 6-digit verification OTP (no session cookie until verified).
- `POST /auth/login` → email/password login; sends a 6-digit sign-in OTP (no session cookie until verified).
- `POST /auth/link-public-key` 🔒 → link wallet address to account.
- `POST /auth/forgot-password` → issue a reset token and email a reset link (`PasswordResetEmail` template); always 200 to avoid email enumeration. Returns the token in non-production for local testing.
- `POST /auth/forgot-password-otp` → email a 6-digit password-reset OTP; always 200.
- `POST /auth/reset-password` → consume a valid reset token, set the new password hash, revoke outstanding reset tokens.
- `POST /auth/reset-password-otp` → consume a valid password-reset OTP.
- `POST /auth/verify-email-otp` → verify a 6-digit email OTP, set session cookie, and set `users.email_verified_at` when applicable.
- `POST /auth/resend-email-otp` → resend the email verification OTP.
- `POST /auth/logout` 🔒 → revoke session.
- `GET  /auth/me` 🔒 → current user (session fields only; `avatarUrl` is always `null` — use `GET /users/me` for avatar).

### users `[MVP]`
- `GET   /users/me` 🔒 → full profile for the signed-in user (includes avatar).
- `GET   /users/:identifier` → public profile by wallet address or nickname.
- `PATCH /users/me` 🔒 → update own profile.

### analysis-requests `[MVP]`
- `POST  /analysis-requests` 🔒 → create analysis request.
- `GET   /analysis-requests` → list (filter `status`).
- `GET   /analysis-requests/me` 🔒 → current user's requests.
- `PATCH /analysis-requests/:id` 👑 → update status / review notes.

### projects `[MVP]`
- `GET  /projects` → list (filters: `state`, `chainId`, `q`, `page`, `limit`).
- `GET  /projects/:slug` → project detail (+ latest score).
- `POST /projects` 👑 → create project.
- `PATCH /projects/:id` 👑 → update.
- `POST /projects/:id/transition` 👑 → change lifecycle state.
- `POST /projects/submit` 🔒 → community submission. `[Phase 2]`

### comments `[MVP]`
- `GET    /projects/:id/comments` → list (paginated).
- `POST   /projects/:id/comments` 🔒 → create.
- `DELETE /comments/:id` 🔒 → soft-delete own.

### voting `[MVP]` (legacy)
- `GET /projects/:id/votes` → legacy public vote tally (deprecated).
- `GET /projects/:id/votes/eligibility?address=` → legacy eligibility (deprecated).

### scoring `[MVP]`
- `GET /projects/:id/score` → current score + breakdown.
- `GET /projects/:id/score/history` → per-round scores.

### governance `[MVP]`
- `GET /governance/proposals` → list (filter `state`).
- `GET /governance/proposals/:onchainId` → detail + votes.

### reputation `[MVP → Phase 1]`
- `GET /reputation/:address` → reviewer credentials (+ factors `[Phase 1]`).

### rewards / notifications `[Phase 1]`
- `GET /rewards/:address`, `GET /notifications` 🔒, `POST /notifications/:id/read` 🔒.

### platform
- `GET /openapi.json` + Swagger UI at `/docs`. `[MVP]`
- `GET /health` → liveness/readiness. `[MVP]`
- `POST /webhooks/subscriptions` 🔒. `[Phase 3]`

## Zod Schemas (representative)

> Schemas live in each module's `*.schema.ts` and are the single source for
> validation + OpenAPI. Examples (TypeScript, Zod):

```ts
// modules/projects/projects.schema.ts  [MVP]
export const ProjectStateSchema = z
  .enum(['in_analysis', 'under_review', 'report_published'])
  .openapi('ProjectState')

export const ProjectSchema = z.object({
  id: z.uuid(),
  slug: z.string(),
  name: z.string().min(1).max(120),
  description: z.string().nullable().optional(),
  chainId: z.number().int(),
  tokenAddress: z.string().nullable().optional(),
  state: ProjectStateSchema,
  votingContractAddress: z.string().nullable().optional(),
  score: z.number().optional(),
  createdAt: z.iso.datetime(),
}).openapi('Project')

export const CreateProjectBodySchema = z.object({
  name: z.string().min(1).max(120),
  description: z.string().optional(),
  chainId: z.number().int(),
  tokenAddress: z.string().optional(),
}).openapi('CreateProjectBody')

export const ListProjectsQuerySchema = z.object({
  state: ProjectStateSchema.optional(),
  chainId: z.coerce.number().int().optional(),
  q: z.string().optional(),
  page: z.coerce.number().int().min(1).default(1),
  limit: z.coerce.number().int().min(1).max(100).default(20),
})
```

```ts
// modules/auth/auth.schema.ts  [MVP]
export const NonceBodySchema = z.object({ address: z.string() })
export const VerifyBodySchema = z.object({
  message: z.string(),
  signature: z.string(),
})
export const SessionUserSchema = z.object({
  id: z.uuid(),
  walletAddress: z.string(),
  role: z.enum(['user', 'team', 'admin']),
})

// modules/comments/comments.schema.ts  [MVP]
export const CreateCommentBodySchema = z.object({
  body: z.string().min(1).max(5000),
})

// modules/governance/governance.schema.ts  [MVP]
export const ProposalSchema = z.object({
  onchainId: z.string(),
  proposerAddress: z.string(),
  title: z.string(),
  description: z.string().optional(),
  state: z.enum(['pending', 'active', 'succeeded', 'defeated', 'executed']),
})
```

## Conventions

- One module = one folder under `modules/`, with `*.routes.ts`, `*.service.ts`,
  `*.repository.ts`, `schemas/` (Zod) and `__tests__/*.test.ts`.
- All request/response shapes validated with Zod; schemas feed OpenAPI.
- DB access only through Kysely repositories; migrations live in `core/db/migrations`.
- On-chain reads only through `core/chain` (Viem); never read RPC from a module directly.
- Tests with Vitest + Supertest, mirroring module layout. `[MVP]`
